Internship as part of the Master's degree program in Educational Technology at Concordia University: The deliverable for “Leading Change” was to design and develop an informal learning environment for employees of the Department of National Defence. Furthermore, the objective was to provide learners with an infrastructure using social media tools available to government employees (GCPedia, GCForums), with which they could build their knowledge, skills, and attitudes on how to manage and lead a change in their organization. The project charter included deliverables such as a literature review of informal learning theory, design proposal, supplemental materials, and both formative and summative evaluation plans. Throughout the design and development of “Leading Change”, close work and partnership with subject matter experts in change management and organizational development ensured the sharing of expert knowledge and skills.

- Designed and developed an adult informal learning environment for employees in Department of National Defence;
